' Cross-deploy funding by the owner of a stored continuation (DR-68, implemented by DR-135).
' Under P1 uniform signing and Rule 4, an installer's unsigned trigger carries the
' installer's region. A later deploy that fires the trigger pays its own side of the
' COMM. The installer, the owner of the stored continuation, pays its side of the COMM
' and the work of the fired body, at the price that its stored region recorded, from
' its owner purse and within its owner budget. An interaction that the owner cannot
' pay does not fire, and the run records the refusal for replay.
'
' Source of truth: docs/casper/theory/cost-accounting-decision-records.md (DR-68, DR-135);
'                  publications/cost-accounting/cost-accounted-rho.tex
'                  (sec:rewrites Rules 1-5, def:sugar-uniform, def:sugar-lollipop, def:funding-proof).
' Palette:  clients = supply blue · runtime = process lilac · funding = gate teal
'           installer purse = pool green · gateway purse = capability indigo
'           debit = red arrows · authorization = blue arrows
' Render:  plantuml -tsvg docs/casper/theory/diagrams/installer-funded-continuation-sequence.puml
'          (or: ./render.sh installer-funded-continuation-sequence.puml)

@startuml installer-funded-continuation-sequence
!include palette.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor $ca_neutral
  LifeLineBorderColor #666666
  ParticipantBorderColor #333333
  BoxBorderColor #999999
}
title Stored continuation funded by its owner's purse (DR-68, DR-135)

actor "Installer\n(owner)" as Installer $ca_supply
actor "Gateway client" as Gateway $ca_supply
participant "Proposer and\nvalidators" as Node $ca_gate
participant "Reducer and RSpace\nwith the owner binding" as Reducer $ca_process
participant "Installer\nowner purse" as InstallerPurse $ca_pool
participant "Gateway\nsigned sources" as GatewayPurse $ca_capability

== Installation (earlier block) ==
Installer -> Node : offered deploy signed by the installer,\nat the installer's signed price
Node -> Reducer : execute the installer's term
Reducer -> Reducer : store the trigger continuation with the installer's\nregion, which records the installer's price

== Trigger (later block, batch member i) ==
Gateway -> Node : offered deploy signed by the gateway
Node -[$ca_instantiate]-> InstallerPurse : read the balance at <latex>R_{i-1}</latex> for the owner table:\nbudget = cap(balance, later holds) minus own hold
Node -> Reducer : execute the gateway's term with the owner table
Reducer -> Reducer : the gateway's send matches the stored trigger
Reducer -> Reducer : owner share = usage times the installer's recorded price
alt the installer's remaining budget covers its share
  Reducer -> Reducer : the COMM fires, and the body runs for its owner,\nthe installer (or for the transferee of a lollipop or slot)
  Node -[$ca_debit]-> InstallerPurse : owner row: the installer's share of the COMM\nand of its body, at the installer's price
  Node -[$ca_debit]-> GatewayPurse : client row: the gateway's own work and the fee
  Node -> Gateway : receipt (one row per debited purse)
else the installer cannot pay
  Reducer -> Reducer : the interaction does not fire,\nboth items stay stored, and the run continues
  note right of Reducer $ca_note_amber
    No charge for an unfired
    communication (P1 Rule 4 token
    gating). The journal records the
    refusal, and replay checks its
    shortfall.
  end note
  Node -[$ca_debit]-> GatewayPurse : client row: the gateway's own work and the fee
end

note over Node $ca_note_grey
  Validators replay the block: they read every
  listed owner purse at <latex>R_{i-1}</latex> again, check the
  owner table, and check each refusal.
end note

note over InstallerPurse $ca_note_grey
  Genesis continuations carry the Unit
  signature, which maps to no purse,
  so blessed system signers are never charged.
  A signature that anyone can spell
  has no purse and budget 0.
end note

legend bottom
  |= colour |= meaning |
  |<$ca_supply>| signing clients |
  |<$ca_gate>| proposer and validators |
  |<$ca_process>| reducer, native meter and RSpace owner checks |
  |<$ca_pool>| the installer's owner purse (wallet keying, DR-28) |
  |<$ca_capability>| the gateway's signed sources |
  |<$ca_debit>| debit at settlement |
  |<$ca_instantiate>| owner budget read at <latex>R_{i-1}</latex> |
  |= name |= meaning |
  | <latex>R_{i-1}</latex> | the state root before batch member i (DR-65) |
  | cap | the G2 capacity: the balance minus the later holds of the block |
  | owner table | the owner purses that the run consults, each with its budget |
endlegend

@enduml
